.TH "DEVICEORIENTATIONEVENT.REQUESTPERMISSION_STATIC" "3JS" "August 4, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
DeviceOrientationEvent.requestPermission_static \-
DeviceOrientationEvent: requestPermission() static method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]requestPermission()\f[B]\f[R] static method of the
\f[CR]DeviceOrientationEvent\f[R] interface requests the user\(cqs
permission to access device orientation data from the accelerometer and
gyroscope sensors.
It can also request permission to access magnetometer data when absolute
orientation is needed.
This method requires transient activation, meaning that it must be
triggered by a UI event such as a button click.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
DeviceOrientationEvent.requestPermission()
DeviceOrientationEvent.requestPermission(absolute)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]absolute\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A boolean indicating whether absolute orientation data is needed.
When \f[CR]true\f[R], the permission request also includes the
magnetometer sensor.
Defaults to \f[CR]false\f[R].
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with a string which is either
\f[CR]\(dqgranted\(dq\f[R] or \f[CR]\(dqdenied\(dq\f[R].
.SS Exceptions
The returned promise rejects with the following exceptions:
.TP
\f[B]NotAllowedError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
The permission state is \f[CR]\(dqprompt\(dq\f[R] and the calling
function does not have transient activation.
.SH SECURITY
Transient user activation is required.
The user has to interact with the page or a UI element in order for this
feature to work.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Requesting device orientation permission on click
.IP
.EX
document.querySelector(\(dqbutton\(dq).addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, \f[B]async\f[R] () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]if\f[R] (\f[B]typeof\f[R] DeviceOrientationEvent.requestPermission !== \(dqfunction\(dq) {
    \f[I]// The feature is not available, or does not need permission.\f[R]
    \f[B]return\f[R];
  }

  \f[B]const\f[R] permission = \f[B]await\f[R] DeviceOrientationEvent.requestPermission();
  \f[B]if\f[R] (permission === \(dqgranted\(dq) {
    window.addEventListener(\(dqdeviceorientation\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
      console.log(\(gaAlpha: ${event.alpha}\(ga);
      console.log(\(gaBeta: ${event.beta}\(ga);
      console.log(\(gaGamma: ${event.gamma}\(ga);
    });
  }
});
.EE
.SS Requesting absolute orientation permission
When absolute orientation data is needed (e.g., for compass\-based
applications), pass \f[CR]true\f[R] as the \f[CR]absolute\f[R]
parameter.
This additionally requests access to the magnetometer.
.IP
.EX
document.querySelector(\(dqbutton\(dq).addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, \f[B]async\f[R] () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]if\f[R] (\f[B]typeof\f[R] DeviceOrientationEvent.requestPermission !== \(dqfunction\(dq) {
    \f[B]return\f[R];
  }

  \f[B]const\f[R] permission = \f[B]await\f[R] DeviceOrientationEvent.requestPermission(\f[B]true\f[R]);
  \f[B]if\f[R] (permission === \(dqgranted\(dq) {
    window.addEventListener(\(dqdeviceorientationabsolute\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
      console.log(\(gaAbsolute alpha: ${event.alpha}\(ga);
    });
  }
});
.EE
